    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d849">

                <pb facs="0867" n="609" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg609"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/1840</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Page</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-11-04">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 4, 1915, noon.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 2 p. m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3154. Paragraph numbered 13, beginning on <ref target="#pg10">page 10</ref> of
                        note,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d849-f1"/> is not quite clear to me. If it means
                    that the British Government has, as a deliberate Government policy, increased or
                    will increase British trade at the expense of American trade, such an imputation
                    of bad faith has been repeatedly denied by the British Government.</p>
                <p>It occurs to me respectfully to ask whether this be your meaning, and if so,
                    whether the paragraph shall be sent in as it was.</p>
                <p>In view of repeated British denials of foregoing as a Government policy, I wish
                    to be absolutely certain of your meaning, and therefore risk the small delay
                    that this question entails.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Ambassador</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
